\]
whose matrix \(ww^\mathsf T\) has rank one. If \(Q(\mathbf t)\le Ch\) as an ordinary integer throughout the parameter domain, the distinct increments lie in an interval of length \(O(\sqrt h)\). Extra parameters supply multiplicities, not extra distinct \(x\)’s.

On a symmetric box, this follows directly from
\[
\max_{\lvert t_i\rvert\le T_i}|w\cdot t|
=\sum_i|w_i|T_i.
\]
Thus the claimed higher-dimensional volume gain is **false for this construction**. Requiring only modular smallness of \(Q\) restores the original nonlinear search problem. CRT-separated nonunit coefficients can evade the integer argument, but their gcds already expose factors.

